AB  - Blockchain technology has emerged as the backbone of cryptocurrencies and decentralized finance, yet its long-term resilience is increasingly threatened by advances in quantum computing. Quantum algorithms, such as Shorβ€™s algorithm, can undermine public-key cryptography, while Groverβ€™s algorithm accelerates brute-force search, weakening proof-of-work schemes. In this paper, we propose a Quantum Blockchain Framework that integrates quantum communication protocols, quantum consensus mechanisms, and quantum-resistant cryptography. We construct a theoretical model of quantum-secured distributed ledgers, where qubits, entanglement, and quantum key distribution (QKD) enhance security and efficiency. Applications to cryptocurrency are explored, highlighting how quantum blockchain can mitigate security risks, improve consensus speed, and enable quantum-native digital assets. Β© 2025 by the author.
