AB  - Artificial intelligence(AI) and blockchain are transformative technologies reshaping the security paradigm in the financial sector. This chapter explores the synergistic integration of AI with blockchain technology to address pressing security challenges, including fraud prevention, data integrity, and regulatory compliance. AI enhances blockchain capabilities through advanced anomaly detection, predictive analytics, and intelligent decision-making, while blockchain ensures data transparency, immutability, and decentralized control. The research delves into the foundational principles of both technologies, their convergence, and the resulting innovations that drive secure financial operations. Real-world implementations such as AI-powered fraud detection systems, smart contract audits, and decentralized identity management highlight the potential of this integration to revolutionize financial services. Additionally, future trends like quantum-resistant algorithms, decentralized AI marketplaces, and AI-governed DAOs are examined to showcase the evolving landscape of secure financial systems. This study concludes by addressing the implications, challenges, and opportunities of adopting AI-based blockchain technologies in financial security. The findings contribute to a deeper understanding of how these technologies can collaboratively create robust, scalable, and sustainable security frameworks for the financial sector. Β© 2026 selection and editorial matter, Alex Khang individual chapters, the contributors.
