AB  - The swift development of quantum computing, which offers previously unheard-of processing power and problem-solving abilities, has the potential to completely transform a number of industries. The revolutionary role of quantum computing in banking, consumer behaviour analysis, block-chain security, digital marketing optimization, and stock market forecasting is examined in this chapter. Quantum algorithms in finance improve fraud detection, portfolio optimization, and risk modeling. Using quantum algorithms like Groverβ€™s algorithm for search optimization and Shorβ€™s algorithm for factorization, we explore how quantum computing can improve stock market forecasting accuracy, optimize consumer insights, secure block chain transactions, personalize digital marketing strategies, and improve financial modeling. Quantum machine learning (QML) provides insights into consumer behaviour by enabling predictive analytics and hyper-personalized suggestions. Blockchain technology ensures data security in decentralized finance (DeFi) by gaining quantum-resistant cryptographic frameworks. While stock market forecasts are improved using quantum-enhanced Monte Carlo simulations and financial modeling, digital marketing tactics use quantum optimization for dynamic pricing and targeted advertising. This chapter illustrates how quantum computing is changing decision-making procedures and computational efficiency in several fields by looking at practical implementations and future possibilities. This article attempts to offer a thorough grasp of the effects of quantum computing on the digital economy and its ramifications for further research and industrial applications through a multidisciplinary lens. Β© The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
