AD  - Marwadi University, Department of Computer Engineering, Gujrat, Rajkot, India
AB  - The conventional method for registering sale deeds in real estate relies heavily on documentation, a single point of control, manual authentication steps, and verification, leading to a myriad of delays, inefficiencies, and susceptibility to fraudulent activities. This framework is further augmented with the introduction of BESDR (Blockchain Enabled Sale Deed Registration), which leverages blockchain technology to enhance the BESDR framework through the decentralization of transaction systems, secure transactions, and provide transparent procedures for the entire property. Eliminating the need for intermediaries and placing trust in stakeholders, the model utilizes smart contracts to automate ownership transfer within the proposed model after successful payment verification. Further proof against evolving cybersecurity threats, BESDR with advanced data protection, integrates NTRUEncrypt, a quantum-resistant cryptographic algorithm. The framework remains structured around user registration, asset registration, and the transfer of assets, enabling synthesis through three core processes executed in Solidity using the Remix IDE BESDR. Evaluation of system performance indicates that the proposed protocol enables a 40% reduction in total processing time, accompanied by a 35% reduction in transactional costs. BESDR also maintains superior communication efficiency while increasing operational simplicity alongside enhanced security standards. A comprehensive scan of land registry systems based on blockchain technology reveals BESDR's unparalleled ability in data relevance, superseding the rest as a primary resistant measure alongside resilience to quantum threats. This study has also addressed gaps such as stakeholder acceptance, infrastructure readiness, and legal compliance frameworks. Future work will investigate the incorporation of AI for dynamic asset valuations and the interfacing with government land registries for practical applications.  Β© 2025 IEEE.
