AB  - The emergence of quantum computing presents existential threats to classical cryptographic protocols, challenging the security foundations of document management systems in sensitive institutional environments. This paper proposes a standards-driven model for document lifecycle management, integrating post-quantum cryptographic mechanisms aligned with the NIST PQC framework and ISO 15489-1 guidelines for recordkeeping. The study outlines redesigned processes that reinforce authenticity, integrity, confidentiality, and granular access control through quantum-resilient primitives. By replacing fragmented manual workflows with a unified, auditable, and future-proof repository, the model ensures compliance with evolving information security standards and regulatory mandates, offering a scalable blueprint for secure digital governance, applicable across various document management environments and, more broadly, in all domains where information asset management is critical.  Β© 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
