AB  - This paper proposes a modular architecture for secure and privacy-preserving data sharing in decentralized environments, combining client-side encryption, decentralized storage, and blockchain-based access control. The solution, TRAIL - Trustworthy Resource Access and Immutable Linking, enforces data confidentiality and traceability through symmetric encryption, asymmetric key encapsulation, and smart contracts for verifiable metadata management. Implemented within a platform that fosters innovation, the architecture enables users to encrypt sensitive information locally, store it via contentaddressable systems like InterPlanetary File System, and selectively grant access through blockchain-anchored encrypted keys. A formal model of the encryption and sharing process is presented, alongside a use-case implementation involving mentorinnovator collaboration. Results demonstrate low-latency key sharing and end-to-end confidentiality without platform-level data exposure. The design is extensible toward post-quantum encryption schemes and identity-based policies, providing a robust foundation for secure digital ecosystems. Β© 2025 IEEE.
