AB  - Anonymous credential schemes are a key application in modern cryptography. Recent research has advanced these schemes by incorporating issuer-hiding capabilities, which prevent the disclosure of the credential issuer's identity. While several issuer-hiding anonymous credential schemes exist, none offer resilience against quantum computing adversaries. To address this gap, we propose a post-quantum issuer-hiding anonymous credential scheme, building on the recent work known as ring referral (S&P '25), which allows anonymous signatures from third-party signers. Ring referral is an integration of ring signature and anonymous credential schemes, enabling issuer-hiding anonymous credentials. In this paper, we present an efficient lattice-based ring referral scheme, which supports quantum-resistant security. Our scheme extends a recent lattice-based credential scheme (CCS '24) via LNP proof system (CRYPTO '22).  Β© 2025 Copyright is held by the owner/author(s). Publication rights licensed to ACM.
