AB  - This paper proposes a lightweight, post-quantum blockchain framework for secure and deniable military communications by steganographically embedding transaction hashes into noisy RF/audio channels. We leverage TinyML models to encode/decode hashes on edge devices (e.g., soldier radios, micro-drones), achieving stealth against adversarial detection while consuming low power. Our consensus mechanism, Proof-of-Steganography, validates transactions only if nodes can extract hidden challenges, eliminating energy-intensive mining. This consensus mechanism can also be used to sync the private key in tactical scenarios such as battlefield communication, surveillance drones, naval fleet coordination, forward-operating sensor grids, and even emergency-response teams-where maintaining device integrity and trust is critical. Β© 2025 IEEE.
