AB  - Surveillance systems like CCTVs help in security as a way of preventing crime, but they are also prone to possible threats like data breaches, unauthorized access to data, and data manipulation. The research examines the challenges of CCTV, including cybersecurity, and proposes intelligent mitigation strategies. To address these threats, a machine learning-based intrusion detection system (IDS) is used for real-time detection. Moreover, for systems to stop or minimize unauthorized alterations, the summation of blockchain technology is enabled to ensure CCTV integrity. The past methods of threat alarming and detection are highly insufficient in refuting and challenging intellectual cyber threats, and here is where Artificial Intelligence (AI) comes in, offering a positive and most suitable solution for real-time cybersecurity issues, with the help of algorithms that detect and identify errors or malfunctions within a system operation and network traffic. AI operates at a very high speed in identifying and providing solutions to complex problems, utilizing search algorithms and optimization techniques to find the best and most satisfying results from a set of commands. As the era of AI is growing incrementally, the blockchain system is not standing still. Since there is a combination of AI and blockchain, the technological systems have accelerated, as the unity has brought data integrity, especially where cryptographic foundations like RSA and ECC are threatened by quantum computing. Blockchain enables trustworthy AI, where the data used in AI can be verified, thereby enhancing secure data exchange and integrity. Real-time monitoring is one of the key benefits of anomaly detection and quantum systems, which utilize efficient and robust algorithms and infrastructure to process data quickly and accurately, following model training and optimization. The use of quantum-resistant cryptography ensures that the data logged remains intact, even in the face of potential threats. Therefore, this system integrates surveillance technology, ranging from intelligent data analysis to cryptography, which is more secure against human interference. It is imperative in governance, businesses, and other sectors of the economy. These sectors require secure monitoring and transparency, making the era of AI and quantum computing a crucial time for data management systems. Β© 2025 IEEE.
