AB  - This chapter investigates the transformative potential of integrating quantum computing and blockchain technology to enhance fraud detection and bolster risk management in financial systems. As digital transactions become more complex and vulnerable to quantum-based threats, conventional security methods are increasingly inadequate in detecting fraud and managing risks effectively. Quantum computing, leveraging principles like superposition and entanglement, in combination with the decentralized framework of blockchain, presents robust solutions to these challenges. The chapter covers fundamental concepts in quantum computing and blockchain, emphasizing crucial algorithms such as quantum machine learning and quantum-resistant cryptography, which optimize fraud detection mechanisms. Several case studies demonstrate practical applications, including using quantum algorithms to increase fraud detection accuracy and blockchain for maintaining secure, immutable transaction records. While integrating quantum and blockchain technologies holds great promise, challenges such as technological scalability, high computational costs, and integration with existing financial infrastructures remain. Despite these hurdles, ongoing advancements suggest that quantum-blockchain systems will significantly improve the resilience of fraud detection and risk management in financial networks. This chapter provides an in-depth overview of the current state and future prospects of this emerging field. Β© 2026 selection and editorial matter, Pushan Kumar Dutta, Pronaya Bhattacharya, Jai Prakash Verma, Ashok Chopra, Neel Kanth Kundu and Khursheed Aurangzeb; individual chapters, the contributors.
