AB  - The evolution of 6G networks is set to revolutionize the concept of smart cities by enabling ultra-fast connectivity, ultra-reliable low-latency communication (URLLC), and enhanced security to meet the rising demand for intelligent urban services. As cities become increasingly interconnected, 6G will serve as the backbone of a security-focused ecosystem, integrating AI, blockchain, the Internet of Things (IoT), edge computing, and quantum communication to optimize service delivery, enhance automation, and ensure robust cybersecurity. This chapter explores the key components of an integrated 6G smart city infrastructure, evaluating how these emerging technologies contribute to the efficiency, reliability, and security of smart services. Future use cases, including intelligent transportation, advanced healthcare, and autonomous systems, are discussed, alongside the challenges and mitigation strategies for securing data-driven urban ecosystems. The study further examines cybersecurity threats associated with 6G networks, addressing concerns such as data privacy risks, AI-driven cyberattacks, and quantum-safe encryption mechanisms. By providing insights into cutting-edge communication and data protection techniques, this chapter contributes to a deeper understanding of technological advancements and their impact on the management and security of 6G-powered smart cities. The findings aim to support researchers, urban planners, and policymakers in building resilient, intelligent, and future-ready urban environments. Β© 2026 selection and editorial matter, Sushil Kumar Singh, Rajendrasinh B. Jadeja, Ashish Khanna, Pushan Kumar Dutta, and Bal Virdee; individual chapters, the contributors.
