AB  - The rapid adoption of Smart Healthcare Edge Computing Systems has transformed healthcare delivery through real-time patient monitoring, low latency telemedicine, AI-assisted diagnostics, and seamless edge cloud integration. However, this interconnected architecture significantly expands the cybersecurity attack surface, exposing IoMT devices, communication networks, edge AI nodes, and cloud connected EHR systems to sophisticated threats. To address these issues, this paper adopts the STRIDE threat modeling framework to develop a layer wise threat taxonomy spanning six architectural layers-Data Generation, Communication, Edge Computing, Access & Authentication, Cloud Storage, and Community Monitoring layers. Each threat category is systematically mapped to context aware countermeasures including Zero Trust architectures, privacy preserving federated learning, blockchain based auditability, and post quantum cryptographic mechanisms. The proposed dual table representation enhances risk visibility, addresses cross layer attack propagation, and provides a structured, implementation ready foundation for securing next generation smart healthcare infrastructures. Β© 2025 IEEE.
