AB  - Direct Anonymous Attestation (DAA) is a cryptographic protocol that enables users with a Trusted Platform Module (TPM) to authenticate without revealing their identity. DAA has been adapted to Vehicle Ad-hoc NETwork system (VANETs) to offer secure vehicle-to-anything communication (V2X). In this paper, we provide an implementation of the most advanced post-quantum DAA for VANETs with a complete parametrization and benchmark in order to embed this scheme on TPM. Β© 2024 by SCITEPRESS β€“ Science and Technology Publications, Lda.
