AB  - A new form of the hidden discrete logarithm problem, pro-posed as primitive of the post-quantum public-key cryptoschemes, is defined over the 6-dimensional finite non-commutative asso-ciative algebra with a large set of the left-sided global units. The considered computationally difficult problem uses the mu-tual commutativity of the exponentiation operation and homo-morphism mapping defined relatively a fixed unit element of the algebra. The related properties of the introduced algebra are described. Novel public key-agreement and zero-knowledge pro-tocols based on the hidden logarithm problem are introduced as post-quantum cryptoschemes. Β© 2019 by D.N. Moldovyan.
