AB  - In this paper, we propose a lattice-based authentication scheme for IoT technologies such as RFID systems. The security of the proposed scheme is based on ISIS problem which helps to resist to quantum attacks. The proposed scheme satisfies zero-knowledge property. Moreover, the location privacy, unforgeability, scalability and forward secrecy properties are achieved. The proposed scheme also has a resistance to man in the middle, replay and impersonation attacks. Moreover, its efficiency is comparable with the recent studies. Β© 2021 Elsevier Ltd
